## 🧠 Final Cheat Sheet

| Check | Why it matters |
|---|---|
| Same length | Mandatory first check |
| Forward map (`s1` → `s2`) | Ensures consistent replacement |
| Reverse map / Used set (`s2`) | Ensures **no two** `s1` chars share the same `s2` char |
| O(n) time, O(1) space | Efficient and optimal |

> 💡 A quick alternative: transform both strings into a **pattern of first-occurrence indices** (e.g., `"moon"` → `0,1,1,2` and `"feed"` → `0,1,1,2`). If the patterns match → isomorphic. But the two-map method is the most intuitive.

